{
  "slug": "ripplo",
  "name": "Ripplo",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A tight validation loop for app-building agents. Hooks enforce tests pass for user-facing edits; skills to author and run deterministic, backend-aware E2E tests; replay UI shows exactly what happened.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **6 skills** and **5 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (6): `create` (Create a Ripplo end-to-end workflow from the app's typed state schema, starting-state constraints, user actions, and complete declared…), `discover` (Guided codebase crawl to plan Ripplo workflows: map the app's surface, extend its typed state schema and starting-state…), `run` (Run Ripplo e2e tests, diagnose failures, and manage Testing Scope — the whole run→diagnose→report loop), `setup` (Initialize Ripplo from zero: sign in → init → start the daemon → connect state sources and browser…), `start` (Start the `ripplo daemon` background process for this dev session), `tasks` (Pick up Ripplo tasks — open-ended requests anchored to a replay frame/element (fix a bug, change behavior, extend/write…)\n- **Hooks** (5): `SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `PostToolUse`, `PreToolUse`, `Stop`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install ripplo@claude-community` from `ripplo/claude-plugin`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 6,
    "hook": 5
  },
